From: PTT-dev
Subject: [PATCH] ramips: fix ralink-i2s refclk pad-setup register corruption

mt7628_refclk_setup() intends to set bit 5 of sysc reg 0x1364, but writes
"data |= ~(0x1 << 5)" which ORs 0xffffffdf into the register, clobbering
every other bit (GPIO1 pull configuration on MT7628).

Use the intended single-bit OR.

--- a/sound/soc/ralink/ralink-i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ralink/ralink-i2s.c
@@ -737,7 +737,7 @@
 	data &= ~(0x1 << 5);
 	rt_sysc_w32(data, 0x1354);
 	data = rt_sysc_r32(0x1364);
-	data |= ~(0x1 << 5);
+	data |= (0x1 << 5);
 	rt_sysc_w32(data, 0x1364);
 
 	/* set refclk output 12Mhz clock */
